### 🚀 How to Commit and Push This to GitHub Quickly

Run these precise commands in your command line terminal inside your project folder to upload your project with clean commit messages:

```bash
# 1. Initialize local version control tracking
git init

# 2. Add files to the staging index
git add .

# 3. Create initial standard production commit tag
git commit -m "feat: initial release of EduPulse Hub student management frontend architecture"

# 4. Enforce correct branch specification layout mapping
git branch -M main

# 5. Connect your project folder to your blank GitHub repository address
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_REPOSITORY_NAME.git

# 6. Push code to your remote main branch securely
git push -u origin main

```